  "title": "Printed Diamond Sutra of 868 (Dunhuang)",
  "summary": "A woodblock-printed scroll of the Buddhist Diamond Sutra, dated by its colophon to 868 and made for free distribution by Wang Jie on behalf of his parents, was later found in the sealed Library Cave near Dunhuang. It is widely described as the oldest surviving dated printed book.",
  "when": {
    "start": {
      "year": 868
    },
